forth.blk holds 1024 bytes: 1 block of 16 lines of 64 columns
forth.blk as text, its lines numbered (the trailing spaces left out):
 1|( The bonus round: a Forth screen, 16 lines of 64 columns )
 2|( A line longer than 64 columns is cut at the 64th: the rest of
 3|: SQUARE  ( n -- n*n )  DUP * ;
 4|: CUBE  ( n -- n*n*n )  DUP SQUARE * ;
 5|: STARS  ( n -- )  0 ?DO [CHAR] * EMIT LOOP ;
 6|: TRIANGLE  ( n -- )  1+ 1 DO CR I STARS LOOP ;
 7|: COUNTDOWN  ( n -- )  BEGIN DUP . 1- DUP 0= UNTIL DROP ;
 8|
 9|5 TRIANGLE
10|3 CUBE .
11|10 COUNTDOWN
